Z||000000||JBGehling||01-04-2001||04:31 PM||||Ok, here's the situation, I received NO ticket, so there's no points off my license.<BR>  The insurance company is now investigating the wreck and they say, if I can prove that she was over the white line (which will be mind-numbingly easy), it becomes all her fault. Here's what happened, she had JUST pulled out and stopped:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/before.gif"> <BR>you see I couldn't go to the left because of the car, and I couldn't hit her head on because my back would've whipped around and hit the other car, so I tried to go around her, to the right and this is what ended up:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/after.gif"> <BR>Her car was PERFECTLY in line with mine at the site, so where my left front side connected with her car was where the door ends on hers (her car was a mustang). That means the door, and everything ahead of that, were ahead of the white line.<BR>We didn't get any pictures of the cars positions but no-one can really argue the point. We do have pictures of the skid marks and where my car would'v ended up.<P>So, with the damage to the cars (or the position of the damage, rather, and pictures of the skid marks, I think this case is over  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">! I'll tell you what happens.<P>Josh<BR>||||reg||1
